---
title: "Embeddings and reranking"
description: "Resolve QQL vector roles, embed text and images, and choose late-interaction or cross-encoder reranking."
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Vector names answer "which vector?" Vector roles answer "what input shape and
embedding path?" QQL keeps those decisions separate.

| Form | Role |
|---|---|
| `USING semantic` | Resolve role from collection schema |
| `USING semantic AS DENSE` | Explicit dense vector |
| `USING lexical AS SPARSE` | Explicit sparse vector |
| `USING colbert AS MULTI` | Explicit dense multivector |

{% qqlExample title="Offline-explicit vector role" %}
```sql
QUERY 'late interaction' FROM papers USING colbert AS MULTI LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Schema with MULTIVECTOR

Token-level multivector storage uses `MULTIVECTOR` with a comparator. The
example below keeps a dense vector for candidate generation and a 128
dimension multivector for late interaction.

{% qqlExample title="Create multi-vector collection for ColBERT" %}
```sql
CREATE COLLECTION kb_articles (
  dense VECTOR(384, COSINE),
  colbert VECTOR(128, COSINE) WITH HNSW (m = 0) WITH MULTIVECTOR (comparator = 'max_sim')
);
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Direct multivector search

Search a multivector space directly with `USING ... AS MULTI`.

{% qqlExample title="Direct ColBERT token-level search" %}
```sql
QUERY 'late interaction vector retrieval'
FROM kb_articles
USING colbert AS MULTI
WHERE category = 'search'
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Two-stage dense retrieval plus rerank

At scale, retrieve candidates with dense search, then rerank with
late-interaction MaxSim over the prefetched set.

{% qqlExample title="Two-stage prefetch and ColBERT reranking" %}
```sql
WITH
  candidates AS (QUERY 'late interaction vector retrieval' USING dense LIMIT 100)
QUERY RERANK TEXT 'late interaction vector retrieval' MODEL 'colbert-v2'
FROM kb_articles
USING colbert AS MULTI
PREFETCH (candidates)
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Cross-encoder reranking

{% qqlExample title="Host pair scoring" %}
```sql
WITH
  candidates AS (QUERY 'vector compression' USING dense LIMIT 50)
QUERY CROSS RERANK TEXT 'vector compression' MODEL 'bge-reranker-base' ON FIELD abstract
FROM papers
PREFETCH (candidates)
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

Cross reranking reads candidate text from the payload, calls the host pair
scoring capability, and reorders hits client-side. It does not use a Qdrant
multivector target.

## Architecture

| Architecture | Retrieval latency | Storage footprint | Interaction depth | Best used for |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Single dense vector | 1-5 ms | Low (1 vector per doc) | Coarse chunk level | First-stage candidate generation |
| ColBERT late interaction | 10-25 ms | Medium (N vectors per doc) | Fine-grained token MaxSim | High-precision candidate reranking |
| Cross-encoder model | 50-200 ms | None (re-evaluates text) | Full cross-attention | Final top-10 scoring and reranking |
